Kind: ablation
Issue: #414
Takes out: argc as a word on a boot task's entry stack in build_args_and_stack() -- it goes back to four bytes, with argv's pointers at offset 4; crt0 reads words, finds argc implausible and leaves argv empty, and boot_probe, which the kernel starts with no bootstrap in front of it, reads argv[0] at address 0 and is terminated, so entry 0 never says it ran.  Seen before the fix in every boot of entries 0, 1, 7 and 8 of the union's merge test at fef82e45, on omen and OMEGA, under TCG and KVM, and at 28a2d0ff on victus
Run: --entry 0 120 -smp 1
Expect: exception_no_server: terminating task .* exception 1, code\[0\]=0x2 code\[1\]=0x0$

